  "title": "BP's Leadership Shift and Appointment of New Chair",
  "summary": "BP has appointed Ian Tyler as its new chair following the resignation of former chairman Albert Manifold, signaling a strategic shift to refocus on fossil fuel extraction. The appointment comes months after the board faced years of turmoil due to the previous leadership's controversial actions.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "BP appointed Ian Tyler as its new chair immediately following the resignation of Albert Manifold.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tyler, who previously served as a non-executive director on BP's board since April 2025, will take over the role with immediate effect.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The appointment is part of BP's strategy to address years of boardroom turmoil and focus on its fossil fuel operations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
